    "lead": "Trekking to Everest Base Camp is the quintessential high-altitude pilgrimage of the mountaineering world. Covering 130 kilometers through the UNESCO-listed Sagarmatha National Park, this trail guides you from the mountain airstrip of Lukla through ancient Sherpa villages, sacred Buddhist monasteries, and rugged glacial moraines to the foot of the planet's highest summit. Curated by 5x Everest summitter Ang Tshering Sherpa, here is your definitive field guide.",
    "readingTime": "28 min read",
