    "lead": "Everest Base Camp (5,364m) is universally hailed as the crown jewel of high-altitude trekking. But what exactly elevates this 130-kilometer Himalayan journey above every other mountain trail on Earth? From the sacred mythos of Chomolungma and heart-pounding flights into Lukla to vibrant Sherpa monasteries, legendary suspension bridges, and world-class teahouse comfort, here are the 17 definitive reasons why Everest Base Camp remains the undisputed king of world adventures.",
    "readingTime": "28 min read",
    "publishedDateText": "Oct 4, 2026",
