    "lead": "The 12-day Gokyo Lakes Trek is the connoisseur's choice in the Everest region. By diverging from the congested commercial highway to Everest Base Camp, this spectacular route follows the wild Dudh Koshi river canyon through serene rhododendron forests up to an amphitheater of six sacred turquoise glacial lakes. Topped off by an unforgettable sunrise ascent of Gokyo Ri (5,357m)—revealing four 8,000-meter giants simultaneously—and a cultural return via ancient Phortse village, this itinerary delivers Himalayan magic at its finest. Here is our field-tested, day-by-day master itinerary for 2026–2027.",
    "readingTime": "22 min read",
    "publishedDateText": "Oct 4, 2026",
    "publishedDateAttr": "2026-10-04",
    "updatedDateText": "Oct 5, 2026",
    "updatedDateAttr": "2026-10-05",
    "heroImg": "images/gokyo-lakes-trek-itinerary.webp",
    "heroAlt": "Trekkers walking along turquoise Gokyo lake shoreline with snow-capped peaks in the background",
