    "lead": "How much does the Gokyo Lakes trek actually cost in 2027? For a standard 11- to 13-day itinerary, expect a total realistic expense between <strong>$1,250 and $1,850 USD per person</strong> for a fully guided, all-inclusive package with a licensed Sherpa guide, porter, domestic flights, permits, meals, and lodge lodging. Independent trekkers hiring local support can budget around <strong>$950 to $1,300 USD</strong>, while high-end luxury lodge treks featuring private heated rooms and helicopter transfers range from <strong>$3,500 to $5,800 USD</strong>. Because prices in the Gokyo Valley rise substantially with every 500 meters of elevation gained, understanding real line-item costs—from Lukla round-trip flights and Sagarmatha permits to hot showers and boiled drinking water—is critical to planning an accurate 2027 budget.",
    "readingTime": "22 min read",
    "publishedDateText": "Oct 4, 2026",
    "publishedDateAttr": "2026-10-04",
    "updatedDateText": "Oct 5, 2026",
    "updatedDateAttr": "2026-10-05",
