        "answer": "Yes, the Annapurna Base Camp trek is 100% open, fully restored, and safe. ACAP authorities and local communities reconstructed damaged stone footpaths, reinforced suspension bridges, and restored teahouse utilities within weeks of monsoon rains receding. Trekkers are actively completing the trek daily."
