    "lead": "When is the absolute best time to trek to Annapurna Base Camp? The undisputed golden windows are <strong>October to November (Autumn)</strong> and <strong>March to May (Spring)</strong>. Autumn brings dry, post-monsoon high-pressure systems with crisp mountain air, flawless azure skies, and incandescent morning alpenglow across the 4,000-meter south face of Annapurna I. Spring follows closely, transforming the lush river canyons and cloud forests below 3,200 meters into an explosion of vibrant red, pink, and white rhododendron blossoms under warm alpine sunshine. However, each season—from the tranquil snows of winter to the challenging summer monsoon—brings distinct trade-offs in temperature, teahouse availability, and avalanche dynamics. Here is our comprehensive, month-by-month guide.",
    "readingTime": "21 min read",
    "publishedDateText": "Oct 4, 2026",
    "publishedDateAttr": "2026-10-04",
    "updatedDateText": "Oct 5, 2026",
    "updatedDateAttr": "2026-10-05",
