        "answer": "No, Annapurna Base Camp is generally considered easier overall than Everest Base Camp because it is lower in altitude (max 4,130 m vs 5,364 m at EBC), shorter in distance (70 km vs 130 km), and does not require flights to Lukla. However, ABC has significantly more steep stone staircases, making it harder on the knees."
