        "content": "\n        <figure class=\"article-figure\">\n          <img src=\"../images/everest-base-camp-trek-cost.webp\" alt=\"A group of foreign trekkers reviewing their map and gear with their Sherpa guide at a high-altitude teahouse lodge in the Khumbu\" class=\"article-figure-img\" width=\"1200\" height=\"700\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n          <figcaption class=\"article-figure-caption\">\n            Planning your Himalayan budget: A realistic financial blueprint for Lukla flights, park permits, teahouse rooms, food, and tipping.\n          </figcaption>\n        </figure>\n        <p>\n          Budgeting for the <strong>Everest Base Camp Trek (5,364m)</strong> can be confusing because quotes on the internet fluctuate wildly—from suspicious \"$700 budget specials\" to luxury lodge itineraries exceeding $5,000.\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          To give you complete clarity, total expedition expenses fall into three distinct travel tiers for 2026–2027:\n        </p>\n        <div class=\"choice-split-grid\">\n          <div class=\"choice-card\">\n            <h3 class=\"choice-card-title\">1. Independent / Guide-Only ($1,050 – $1,300)</h3>\n            <ul>\n              <li>You arrange your own round-trip Lukla flights (~$440) and permits (~$50).</li>\n              <li>You hire a licensed guide ($35/day) or porter-guide through an agency.</li>\n              <li>You pay cash out-of-pocket for all teahouse meals, hot showers, charging, and beds as you hike.</li>\n              <li>Requires careful cash management and handling teahouse bookings independently.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"choice-card\">\n            <h3 class=\"choice-card-title\">2. Standard All-Inclusive Local Package ($1,350 – $1,650)</h3>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>The Sweet Spot for 90% of Hikers:</strong> Booked directly with a licensed Kathmandu agency like Igloo Himalaya Treks.</li>\n              <li>Includes: Round-trip Lukla airfare, airport transfers, all permits, senior Sherpa guide, mountain porter, all 3 daily meals, tea/coffee, and teahouse rooms.</li>\n              <li>Predictable budget, guaranteed rooms during peak season, and 24/7 emergency rescue coordination.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"choice-card\" style=\"margin-top: 20px;\">\n          <h3 class=\"choice-card-title\">3. Luxury Teahouse & Heli Return ($2,800 – $4,500+)</h3>\n          <ul>\n            <li>Features premium luxury lodges (Yeti Mountain Home, Everest Summit Lodges) offering heated electric blankets, en-suite private bathrooms, and gourmet dining in Phakding, Namche, and Deboche.</li>\n            <li>Includes a private helicopter return from Gorak Shep (5,164m) directly back to Lukla or Kathmandu, bypassing the 3-day descent on foot.</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      "
