    "lead": "How much does the Annapurna Base Camp (ABC) trek cost in 2026 and 2027? For a standard 8- to 10-day itinerary, expect a total realistic expense between <strong>$750 and $1,150 USD per person</strong> for an all-inclusive guided package with a licensed guide, porter, ACAP permits, private 4WD trailhead jeep transfers, teahouse lodging, and three daily meals. Independent trekkers organizing local logistics can budget around <strong>$500 to $750 USD</strong>, while luxury lodge treks featuring private rooms and chartered helicopter returns directly from ABC to Pokhara range from <strong>$1,800 to $3,200 USD</strong>. Because the Annapurna region eliminates expensive mountain flights, it remains one of the best-value premier treks in the world. Here is your definitive line-item financial guide.",
