    "quickAnswerTitle": "Quick Answer: What You Need to Know About Annapurna Base Camp Trek Cost 2026",
    "quickAnswerContent": "\n    <p><strong>Trailhead & Elevation:</strong> The classic trek departs from Nayapul or Ghandruk near Pokhara, climbing through the Modi Khola canyon to Machhapuchhre Base Camp (3,700m) and the Annapurna Sanctuary bowl at 4,130m.</p>\n    <p><strong>Permits Required:</strong> Annapurna Conservation Area Project (ACAP) permit (NPR 3,000 / ~$23 USD) plus Trekkers' Information Management System (TIMS) card (NPR 2,000 / ~$15 USD).</p>\n    <p><strong>Trail Atmosphere & Physical Demand:</strong> Famous for thousands of hand-cut stone steps between Tikhedhungga, Ulleri, and Chhomrong. Rated moderate-to-strenuous; requires solid knee stability and cardiovascular endurance.</p>\n    <p><strong>Safety Precaution:</strong> The narrow gorge between Deurali (3,200m) and MBC (3,700m) passes several known avalanche chutes. Always listen to guide instructions and check daily snow conditions before crossing.</p>\n  ",
