        "q": "How do I get safe drinking water without buying single-use plastic bottles?",
        "a": "Single-use mineral water bottles are heavily discouraged and increasingly banned along the trail. Instead, order boiled water from teahouses (NPR 150–300 per liter) or treat tap water using a portable SteriPEN UV purifier or chlorine dioxide purification tablets (Aquatabs / Micropur) inside your reusable wide-mouth Nalgene bottles."
