    "heroAlt": "Top 10 travel and trekking destinations in Nepal scenic landscape panorama",
    "heroCaption": "From towering Himalayan giants to ancient UNESCO royal squares and wild subtropical jungles, Nepal delivers unmatched natural and cultural wonders.",
    "quickAnswerTitle": "Quick Answer: What Are the Top 10 Destinations in Nepal?",
    "quickAnswerContent": "\n    <p><strong>The Top 10 Highlights:</strong> Nepal's definitive destinations span <strong>Kathmandu Valley</strong> (UNESCO heritage & living culture), <strong>Pokhara</strong> (adventure capital & serene Phewa Lake), <strong>Everest Region / Khumbu</strong> (the foot of Sagarmatha), <strong>Annapurna Region</strong> (sanctuaries & world-class circuits), <strong>Chitwan National Park</strong> (wild one-horned rhinos & tigers), <strong>Upper Mustang</strong> (the ancient walled Tibetan kingdom), <strong>Langtang Valley</strong> (sacred glacial valleys & Tamang resilience), <strong>Manaslu Circuit & Tsum Valley</strong> (untamed remote Himalayan wilderness), <strong>Rara Lake</strong> (Nepal's largest alpine mirror in the Far West), and <strong>Lumbini</strong> (the sacred birthplace of Lord Buddha).</p>\n    <p><strong>Best Time to Visit:</strong> High-altitude treks peak in <strong>Autumn (October–November)</strong> and <strong>Spring (March–May)</strong> with crystal-clear skies. <strong>Upper Mustang</strong> is ideal during the summer monsoon (June–August) thanks to its rain-shadow geography. Cultural and wildlife hubs like <strong>Kathmandu, Pokhara, Chitwan, and Lumbini</strong> are marvelous from October through March.</p>\n    <p><strong>Ideal Trip Duration:</strong> A classic cultural & safari circuit (Kathmandu + Pokhara + Chitwan) requires <strong>8–10 days</strong>. Combining cultural highlights with a premier trek (EBC, Annapurna Base Camp, or Langtang) requires <strong>14–18 days</strong>.</p>\n  ",
    "quickAnswerCtaText": "Planning a customized journey across Nepal's top destinations?",
