    "quickAnswerContent": "\n    <p><strong>The Top 10 Routes:</strong> Nepal's premier trekking routes encompass <strong>Everest Base Camp</strong> (the world's flagship mountain journey), <strong>Annapurna Circuit</strong> (unmatched ecological diversity crossing Thorong La), <strong>Manaslu Circuit</strong> (the top wild alternative to Annapurna), <strong>Annapurna Base Camp</strong> (a 360° glacial amphitheater), <strong>Langtang Valley</strong> (closest alpine culture without internal flights), <strong>Gokyo Lakes</strong> (emerald waters & 4 eight-thousander vistas), <strong>Mardi Himal</strong> (best rapid 5-day ridge trek), <strong>Upper Mustang</strong> (the trans-Himalayan forbidden kingdom), <strong>Everest Three Passes</strong> (the ultimate high-altitude endurance loop), and <strong>Kanchenjunga Circuit</strong> (untamed far-eastern pioneer wilderness).</p>\n    <p><strong>Key 2026 Regulations:</strong> The Nepal Tourism Board (NTB) strictly mandates <strong>certified, licensed guides for all foreign trekkers</strong> in national parks and conservation areas. Solo unguided trekking is prohibited. High-altitude Starlink satellite Wi-Fi and solar charging are now widely accessible in modern lodges.</p>\n    <p><strong>Best Trekking Windows:</strong> Autumn (October–November) offers crystal-clear skies and stable high-altitude conditions. Spring (March–May) brings warming temperatures and blooming rhododendron forests. Upper Mustang is the premier summer monsoon (June–August) rain-shadow choice.</p>\n  ",
